<v SPEAKER_2>Did you ever feel when remote viewing, you were being watched or something was viewing you? Like you're tapped into a stream of information that something else was aware you were there?

01:37:29.171 --> 01:45:08.831
<v SPEAKER_1>Oh, I know that. In fact, you'd be very interested in this because it had to do with me targeting a UFO. I don't generally target UFOs. The reason I don't is because there's no ground truth. But I can't select my own target, so I wind up targeting them occasionally. Most of the time, they were machines. To be honest, they're machines. Even if there were entities inside, they weren't what I would call intelligent entities. They were programmed entities. You know, the alien robots are live. We build robots out of machines. So a lot of the people that they say are obviously aliens of different descriptions, they're just simply grown in a lab and they're programmed to do certain things. It's the reason they have so much indifference towards us. They're robots for any other work. But I got targeted on the one UFO one time many years ago, maybe 20 years ago. And as soon as I opened to the target, I was recognized as penetrating an area I shouldn't have been in. I was able to capture maybe two glimpses perceptibly and a shutdown. And part of it worried me because whatever entity was in that UFO knew instantly that I was there from a mental standpoint. And so I was concerned that there might be retribution for that. But the retribution turned out to be interesting because every time I went back and I did, I went back to that target a number of times with the idea that maybe I'll catch them off guard. No, you don't. Every time I went back to that target, I would get the same information. So for six months, I got the same thing over and over and over and over again. And what it was, I don't know if you remember the old Vietnam peace symbol. It was a line down like this and then two lines under it. Okay, like an upside down Y. But it was in a circle. Well, that upside down Y is all I could get for six months. And I tried to figure out what is it connected to? What does it mean? How is it used? Is it a symbol for something? Is it this that I couldn't get any further with? And one day I had an epiphany. You know what that is? That's the inside and outside corner of an empty box. As soon as I concluded that, it went away. And it was replaced by three boxes. Now I get three boxes for another six months, stacked all different ways, but they're all equal. They all look the same. They just are never perceived in the same positions. They move around. They change all the time. So I dealt with that for quite a while. I can't even remember how long. And then suddenly, that changed. Because I had another epiphany. I remembered when I was a little kid, my parents gave me three blocks. And they were wrapped in plastic. I did the plastic with three blocks, and it had letters. A, B, C, D, E, F, G, on one, H, I, J, K on the other. And numbers on the other with the ends of the alphabet. So it was the alphabet and the numbers. And I was supposed to learn numbers and alphabet from it. Okay? As soon as I realized that, now I get multiple blocks. I'm getting sometimes seven, sometimes 11, sometimes three. Multiple blocks with a single symbol on it. Now, why is that happening? I think I'm supposed to try to figure out what the symbol represents. And that's what I'm working on now. But this is a slow process. This has been going on for five years. So what is that all about? I suspect, and this is, again, this is information that has come along with the processing that I do in my head. The information I'm getting is there's no way that whatever civilization that entity comes from, we're never gonna know that entity. And here's the reason why. There are a half a million years ahead of us. So on one side, you got this group of entities, a half a million years ahead. And on this side, you got a lot of immature people. That's us, okay? We do things because we can, not because we should, okay? If those two groups ever came together, it would destroy both. There's just no way we'd ever get along. We'd want what they have, and they wouldn't want us to have it. Right there, eradicating conflict. They'd have to put us down. It just can't happen. I understand that. So I think they're viewing what they're doing with me as a way of maybe teaching, and all my thinking about the way the target changes or improves. I'm also getting a lot of feeling about why. You know, why not? Why yes, why of, why because, all those kinds of things. And I don't like it because I feel like I'm being controlled. But I can understand why. Because we're a dangerous species. Yep. Here's my fear. All, you know, less than a hundred years ago in America, we were in covered wagons going west. We didn't have a country yet. And in truth, we were still dividing up into states and stuff, or settling in the west and creating new businesses and things. We're still a growing, changing world because humans, hopefully, are improving and not dissolving. But however that's happening, the problem I'm having is that our greatest discoveries are accidental. When we discovered the use of nuclear energy to produce a weapon, that's the first thing we did. We went and made a weapon out of it.

01:45:08.831 --> 01:45:09.411
